From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:06:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(battery): sample the day of 24/7 HRV capture, offload
 every 30 min while streaming

24/7 continuous capture now streams the whole nightly window as before and, by
day, 5 of every 30 minutes: a 5-minute R-R window is the standard short-term HRV
reading and the daytime Stress score is HR-only, needing 5 minutes of samples an
hour, so every waking hour keeps two windows while the strap streams a sixth of
the day. While the realtime stream runs, the history offload waits 30 min instead
of 15 (HR and R-R already arrive live; nothing is lost). Arming the stream
restarts the lapse clock so the off spell is not read as a stall. Overnight-only
and live screens are unchanged. The settings copy says so.

Not validated on a strap yet: BLE behaviour cannot be tested off-device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
